    "title": "Unified Consciousness Theory II: Consciousness Theories as Effective Organization Theories",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23008262",
    "publication_date": "2026-09-28",
    "description": "<p>Unified Consciousness Theory II develops a constrained intertheory framework for reconstructing, embedding, reinterpreting, or explicitly conflicting operational substructures of major consciousness theories inside the physically anchored UCT-I mother formalism.</p><p>TA-TR-2026-21, version 1.0. Human author of record and responsible depositor: Hongju Liu. Substantial ChatGPT (OpenAI GPT-5.6 Sol) assistance under human direction. Not peer reviewed.</p><p>The release separates formal recovery from empirical validation, includes bridge-admissibility and translation-fidelity constraints, audits nine target theories, and preserves two fixed-parameter cross-theory toy-model demonstrations. It does not claim V3/V4 empirical recovery, human-data validation, robust whole-theory compression, or proof of UCT-I axioms.</p>",
